      "heading": "Questions",
      "html": "<h3>Is every resident fall reportable under RIDDOR?</h3><p>No. RIDDOR covers work-related harm. A fall from a resident's own frailty is generally not reportable. One caused by how the work was done may be. Check the current HSE guidance each time.</p><h3>What is the difference between RIDDOR and telling the regulator?</h3><p>RIDDOR is a report to the HSE. A notice to CQC or the Care Inspectorate is a separate duty. One incident can need both, one, or neither.</p><h3>Does Quickler decide if an incident is reportable?</h3><p>No. It records the facts and lists the follow-up jobs. You or the registered person decide.</p><h3>Can I check incidents over WhatsApp?</h3><p>Yes. You answer by voice note, text or photo. No app to install. Clinical detail stays in the home's own records.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/care-home-health-safety-audit-uk.html\">Care home health and safety audit</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/care-home-compliance-checklist-monthly-uk.html\">Monthly care home compliance checklist</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/safeguarding-audit-care-home-uk.html\">Safeguarding audit for care homes</a></li></ul>"
